From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riched20: Format the word around the insertion point for SCF_WORD in msftedit's class.

AI-assisted (Claude), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted
upstream.

Windows 10 (x86_64 and i686; winum
docs/wine-repro/riched20-scf-word-insertion-point, windows-2026-11-09 and
windows-2026-11-09-boundary) gives different results for msftedit's class
RichEdit50W and riched20's RichEdit20W:
- msftedit: EM_SETCHARFORMAT(SCF_SELECTION | SCF_WORD) at an empty
  insertion point formats characters only when those on both sides of the
  point are of the same class, and then the run of that class around the
  point: the word (letters, digits, an apostrophe between them), the
  punctuation, or between spaces the word before them with the spaces;
  between a word and a paragraph mark, the mark. At a word start or end,
  next to another class, or at the start of the text only the insertion
  point changes, whatever the character formats.
- riched20 formats words in another way (with the trailing space at a
  word end), which this patch leaves as Wine has it.
- Both: with a selection, SCF_WORD formats the selection only; Wine
  extended it to whole words.

Inventor's text editors are RichEdit50W windows (+win trace: 492 creations,
no RichEdit20W). It sets its normal font with SCF_WORD right after GD&T
symbol letters in another face, a word end; Wine formatted the word, and
the symbols turned into letters.

Wine registers both classes with one window procedure; a flag in the
editor records that the window was created with msftedit's class (case
insensitive, as class names are), and only then the msftedit rule is
used. Windowless text services keep riched20's behaviour. Classes are
decided with iswalnum; other scripts were not measured.

v5 (2026-11-09, after cross review): the class flag is set to FALSE in
ME_MakeEditor (it was left unset for every editor but RichEdit50W
windows); a test creates and destroys both classes in turn in one
process.
v4 (2026-11-09, after cross review of the paired textfont candidate):
the msftedit rule only for RichEdit50W windows, RichEdit20W unchanged
except for selections; the paragraph-mark case added; tests for both
classes (riched20's editor tests for RichEdit20W).
v3 (2026-11-09): msftedit's rule for both classes.
v2 (2026-11-09): three rules derived from riched20 only.

